        "original_id": "11114660-f109-5a87-95dc-c39c5991ce9c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Erlend Øye, Stuart Lee Murdoch\n- Bands: Kings of Convenience, Belle and Sebastian, The Whitest Boy Alive, Hjálmar\n- Music releases: Legao, \"Garota\"\n- Places: Bergen, Norway, Glasgow, Reykjavík, Seoul, Iceland, Scotland\n- Topics: indie folk-pop, indie pop, reggae\n\nFacts:\n- Stuart Lee Murdoch was born on 25 August 1968.\n- Belle and Sebastian are a Scottish band that was formed in Glasgow in January 1996.\n- Kings of Convenience is an indie folk-pop duo from Bergen, Norway.\n- Stuart Lee Murdoch is a Scottish musician, writer, and filmmaker.\n- Stuart Lee Murdoch is the lead singer and songwriter for the indie pop band Belle and Sebastian.\n- Legao is the second solo album by Erlend Øye, who is a singer in Kings of Convenience and The Whitest Boy Alive.\n- Legao was recorded in Reykjavík with Hjálmar, a reggae group from Iceland.\n- The single \"Garota\" preceded Legao, and its videoclip was shot in Seoul.",
